{
  "title": "Second declension: neuter nouns",
  "note": "Second-declension neuters end in -um, genitive -i: bellum, belli (n). Every neuter noun uses the same form for nominative and accusative, and its nominative plural ends in -a: bella, wars; dona, gifts. Some nouns exist only in the plural, such as arma (weapons) and castra (camp).",
